  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for Weather Ready Pacific</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Weather Ready Pacific (WRP) aims for all Pacific nations to have access to localised, accurate and timely forecast and warning products to help communities plan for and respond to weather conditions. This Pacific-led initiative was developed by the Pacific Meteorological Council and endorsed by Pacific Leaders in 2021. WRP has a technical design for a USD 191 million initiative. Australia has committed AUD30 million to the initiative (Foreign Minister Wong, February 2023). An initial AUD3 million grant was provided to the Secretariat of the Pacific Regional Environment Programme (SPREP), the implementation lead, to establish a Program Management Unit (PMU), followed by an agreement of AUD27 million financing implementation, strengthening the establishment and including GEDSI across WRP operations. In addition to the AUD30 million commitment, Australia is funding technical expertise to support the program through the Bureau of Meteorology.</narrative>
  </description>
